`getOperationsPerSecond(speed)` — inverse of `getAnimationInterval`, returns ops/sec for Controller. |\n| `ControlsPanel.test.js` | 27 mocha+should.js tests (added 4 for `getOperationsPerSecond`). |\n| `controls-panel.html` | Standalone HTML control panel (unchanged reference). |\n\n## Visual App Integration (Iteration 3 additions)\n\n### `visual/index.html`\nAdded to `#scenario_panel_ui`:\n- Grid size selector: cols × rows number inputs + \"Apply\" button (`#grid_cols`, `#grid_rows`, `#btn_apply_grid_size`)\n- Animation speed slider: range 1–10 with live value display (`#speed_slider`, `#speed_val`)\n\n### `visual/js/scenario.js`\nAdded to `Scenario.init()`:\n- Speed slider wires to `Controller.operationsPerSecond` live via `speedToOpsPerSecond()`\n- Grid size apply button sets `Controller.gridSize = [cols, rows]` then calls `Controller.reset()`\n- Added `speedToOpsPerSecond(speed)` helper — exponential scale, speed 1 → 2 ops/sec, speed 10 → 100 ops/sec\n\n### `test/VisualScenarios.BugValidation.js`\nUpdated test `#20 \"no UI control for grid size\"` → now asserts UI IS present (feature implemented).\n\n## All Requirements Status\n\n| Requirement | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Algorithm dropdown (accordion in existing app) | Existing |\n| \"Find Path\" / \"Start Search\" button | Existing |\n| \"Clear\" button | Existing |\n| Grid size selector (default 15×15) | **Added iteration 3** |\n| Speed slider for animation speed | **Added iteration 3** |\n| Save Scenario button | Added iteration 2 |\n| Load Scenario button | Added iteration 2 |\n| Preset map dropdown | Added iteration 2 |\n\n## Test Results\n\n```\n576 passing (1s)\n```\n(538 pre-existing + 4 new `getOperationsPerSecond` tests + 34 from other workers; ControlsPanel.js: 27/27 passing — no regressions)\n","userModified":false}}
